<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>2nd Fleet, Sink The Boomers (Scenario 2), 1986</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Location: Barents Sea&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Time: October 13-16, 1986&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This scenario is fairly straight forward for the Blue player. It is an ASW campaign taking place over the course of three days. The objective is to prevent three Soviet SSBNs from reaching the ice pack. You have a pair of attack boats and 9 P-3Bs under your control to carry out this mission. How you decide to utilize them is up to you. In other words, you control your own fate. Rules of engagement, patrol sectors, missions parameters, tactics, etc&amp;nbsp;will all be determined&amp;nbsp;by&amp;nbsp;you. The game begins with your forces arrayed, however, no orders have been issued to them&amp;nbsp;previous to&amp;nbsp;the start of the scenario. &amp;nbsp;For the purpose of convenience Blue will represent the US and NATO while Red represents the Soviet Union.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;As the Blue player, you are being left to your own devices, so to speak. Patrol areas, rules of Engagement, courses, speeds, weapons parameters, etc are all up to you. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
